config PACMAN_SPLASH_STYLE
    string "Which splash goes up at boot"
    default "drawn"
    help
      "drawn" builds it out of the wordmark and the sprites, so every colour
      in it is a setting.  "image" puts up the picture in splash_image.h
      instead, which brings its own eight colours and ignores those settings.

config PACMAN_SPLASH_FRAMES
    int "Ticks the splash screen stays up"
    default 50
    help
      Times PACMAN_SPLASH_INTERVAL.  The default is two and a half seconds,
      which is long enough that LVGL's first flush of its empty screen lands
      on the splash rather than on the game.

